"analyst_adjustment": -2.13, "key_factors": ["D+17 Chicago-area district plus a Democratic-leaning midterm environment", "August poll shows the Democrat leading the Republican 34-15 in the four-candidate field", "Independent rivals were knocked off the ballot, clearing a path for Garcia's succession but fueling machine-politics backlash", "Markets price the Democrat near 96%; Getty's independent bid splits the non-Democratic vote"], "rationale": "The district's D+17 lean, a favorable environment for the incumbent party, and the only recent poll showing the Democrat up 19 over the Republican all point to the seat staying Democratic. The open seat and ballot-access controversy add some risk, but the Republican starts far behind and the independent vote is divided between Getty and Hershey.", "watch": "Whether Chris Getty consolidates the anti-machine vote, with Ed Hershey also on the ballot, or new polling shows the Democrat stalled in the mid-30s.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Newest usable poll is 57 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Chuy García (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Illinois' 4th District is a heavily Democratic Chicago-area seat, D+17, where Representative Chuy Garcia is retiring. Patty Garcia, the retiring congressman's preferred successor, leads the ticket with about $359,000 raised. The field narrowed in July when two independent candidates, including Ald. Byron Sigcho-Lopez, failed to qualify for the ballot, leaving Garcia, Republican Lupe Castillo, independent Chris Getty, and Ed Hershey. The removals drew machine-politics criticism and a lawsuit, but they also cleared a path for the Democratic nominee.\n\nAn August poll of registered voters showed the Democrat at 34 percent and the Republican at 15, a 19-point lead, with Getty and Hershey drawing the remainder. Prediction markets price the Democratic candidate around 96 percent. The district's lean and the midterm environment favor the party holding the seat, though the fragmented field and lingering ballot controversy keep some uncertainty in the outlook.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9927, "margin": 21.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9941, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9922, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9863, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9838, "margin": 20.0}]}